{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "The Focus Board (supabase/migrations/0029_focus_board.sql): an ordered list of open tasks the owner keeps an eye on. A task is on the board when its focus position is set; 'focus' below is that position, null when it is off the board. 'board': the tasks on the board in order: open, not deleted, with a position, by position, then oldest first, then id. 'append': the position a task added at the end gets: one more than the last task's on the board, or 1 when the board is empty. 'placeAt': the position a task gets when it is put at 'place' (1 is the top) of the board, with the task itself left out of the board first: halfway between its new neighbours, one less than the first when it goes to the top, one more than the last when it goes to the end, and 1 on an empty board. A place past the end is the end; a place below 1 is the top. 'candidates': the tasks the add picker offers for 'query', in order: open, not deleted, not on the board, and every word of the query (split on spaces) found in the title or the notes, ignoring case and accents; an empty query keeps them all. They come by their date, the deadline when there is one and the planned day otherwise, earliest first and those without a date last, then by title ignoring case and accents, then by id. Tasks without a 'title' use their id as the title; 'notes', 'day' and 'deadline' are empty when left out.",
